From 09c530426a402038777c87c9682e8ccf82c7e9b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: danielwoz <danielwoz@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 08:36:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Enable full Bambu (BBL) printer handling in OrcaSlicer

Loads the Bambu network plugin and the modern device UI so Bambu printers work
directly from OrcaSlicer: live camera, filament colour change, AMS active drying
(with safe per-filament default temperatures), and SD/internal storage browsing.

On Windows the plugin runs in-process via an Authenticode signature redirect, so
it requires Bambu Studio v2.7.1.57 (latest stable) installed but not running: its
genuine signed binaries are read (never executed) to satisfy the plugin's
signed-host check.

MinHook (for the redirect) is a git submodule at deps/minhook.

Verified end to end on a Bambu H2S.
